++# Original Navigation scene composition (work in progress)
++
++This private owner surrounds the existing Common16 Navigation prefix,
++Continuation, G1 Flow and Origin3. It supplies no alternative recipe, expected
++location, image policy, camera input, new restart or public capability.
++
++Original-retention correction: a later passive audit of 63 evidence folders
++found missing declared world-model directories in 32 earlier GREEN execution
++results (150 missing root entries across all inspected outcomes). Those
++execution results and their actual source-hash checks remain historical facts;
++their complete original retention is UNQUALIFIED. An inherited, previously
++registered bound `Model.close` explicitly removed its temporary directory,
++despite a later replacement of `world.close`. Missing originals are not
++reconstructed or adopted. The exclusive scene fixture now preserves that
++directory before any input while still running the registered close and actual
++socket/thread/OFD cleanup. No historical result is retroactively promoted.
++
++`NavigationScenePrefix` starts one original 120-second clock before its first
++observation. PrimaryPrepare retains the actual hidden UI, independent probe and
++NativeSubject, restorable QString/Settings, original URL and original Session
++before normal Go To A. A fresh completed scene-write receipt is required beyond
++the original provider prefix. Home and Login entry use the existing ordinary
++controls. The same original Prefix then selects its directory normally; a
++normal Close supplies the hidden A baseline. The first Common `open` includes
++its actual ordinary tablet Open before delegating Places Entry to that Prefix.
++
++The immutable preparation bridge records every intervening same-Session
++envelope and its actually sampled neutral status. It never substitutes an
++expected sequence offset. Default directory/bookmark joins still write their
++original versions 1/2. Opt-in TransitJoin3 references this typed bridge.
++
++Primary and Actor retain distinct readers, requests, PNGs and metadata through
++existing NavigationStereo2 owners and existing render-store namespaces. The
++external runner alone decides changed pixels with the unchanged two-eye
++verifier. The scoped host fixture renders the actual loaded authored scene and
++actual HTTP marker through independently projected, clipped native-camera eye
++viewports. It is an explicit software/SDK model, not a native renderer or
++headset qualification.
++
++Generation construction initially binds NavigationSceneIO through the existing
++single-owner APIs. Existing native/controller/Home and Stop/Launch callbacks
++retain all their old work; the pinned original outer fence runs before and
++last after it. No G1 operation gets a fresh original-owner clock or budget.
++
++The raw literal container reuses the selected AudioRawArchive implementation,
++with Navigation-only scope and no audio facts. Every enclosing-family original
++part and actual stored/decoded bytes count toward the same 512-part/16 MiB
++bill. The existing 64 KiB original-file and 48 KiB packed-child bounds remain.
++An already issued raw return is archived before parsing even after expiry or
++loss of business-Parent authority. This grants no new getter or input. Unknown
++append/CAS/OFD ownership remains sticky. Immutable lease, bridge and Origin
++files use the existing ClosedOriginalFile byte/full-stamp read windows.
++
++Version boundaries are explicit:
++
++| Source | Current opt-in writer | Historical reading |
++| --- | --- | --- |
++| Scene owner / pre-setup lease | 2 | Warm owner creation never adopts old WIP |
++| Preparation bridge | 2 | Bridge reader reads 1/2; original version-1 rules remain |
++| Transit join | 3 | Reads 1/2/3; default writers remain 1/2 |
++| G1 directory restoration | 2 | Reads 1/2; default writer remains 1 |
++| Raw literal container | 1 | Original selected range/append semantics unchanged |
++| Optional SDK probe source | 1 | Existing selected helper; bound before any source acquisition |
++| Generation gap ledger | 1 | Private WIP around the same Continuation/Flow |
++| Original-world restoration child | 1 | Warm construction only; no orphan/cold adoption |
++
++Lease2 pins an independently observed controlled original scene base, including
++one different from the stimulus base. Cleanup must construct normal navigation
++for exactly that observed original base. The environment configuration is not
++rewritten. An original URL inside the owned run has no invented post-retirement
++static fallback: final green must remain refused without a valid original
++restoration route.
++
++`NavigationSceneGeneration` is a gap ledger around the same original
++Continuation/Flow. Its directory-restored state does not claim original-world,
++role, resource or host retirement. Those remain explicit outstanding proofs.
++`navigation_scene_state.retained()` blocks generic cleanup for the whole
++target-derived family, including rootless raw/chunk/pending namespaces and a
++forged done flag, before Native/Input/BaseStop calls.
++
++## Evidence so far
++
++The earlier version-1 scoped eleven-action composition passed in 29.166s under
++the unchanged outer 120s, with 193 loaded source byte hashes/full physical
++stamps unchanged. It measured A/B/A independently in both eyes of both roles
++and retained all six stereo originals. The unchanged legacy eleven-action
++owner passed in 8.936s with 176 loaded sources unchanged. Their remaining
++originals and preceding failures remain evidence, but the later audit found
++their declared world-model directories missing. They are not complete-retention,
++current whole G1 or final-retirement qualification.
++
++Subsequent focused proofs retain a permitted incompressible 262144-byte NUL
++literal before the actual Native parser, retain issued late/lost-Parent
++returns, reject capacity before send/getter, reject equal-byte lease inode
++replacement even after a chunks reload, retain unknown neutral status, and
++prevent late final QML/Home publication while preserving issued intent.
++
++Current G1 composition, exact original-world restoration, full independent
++Actor coordination and final resource/host retirement remain work in progress.
++No device campaign, build, compiler or public feature completion is claimed.
++
++The current original-root seal reuses only the JSON interpretation admitted
++after a successful original CAS readback. Every access still uses a fresh
++`observer_return.raw_file` OFD window and reads all current bytes/full physical
++identity. The original committed memory object, its fresh canonical contents,
++the immutable seal tuple and byte identity must match. It does not reuse a
++current file, ownership or deadline verdict. Thirteen affected cases passed in
++16.596s with all 194 loaded source hashes/full physical stamps unchanged;
++these include actual byte/inode/memory/seal replacement and recycled-FD
++counterexamples, ordinary preparation, late final input and issued raw return
++retention. On one fresh actually prepared owner, six balanced batches of 30
++actual filesystem root checks per method measured 715.6 us before and 174.8 us
++after. This is a method measurement, not a whole-flow result.
++
++The following continuous current-source 15/G1 attempt remained RED at the
++original 120-second bound. It completed the fifteen normal actions, retained
++all six preceding role A/B/A stereo originals and saved the first actual G1
++stereo source, then expired during that source's original receipt-retirement
++inspection. Both G1 role frames and directory/original-world restoration are
++not qualified. All 271 loaded source hashes/full physical stamps were
++unchanged. The terminal audit inventoried 151 remaining files (925,784 stored
++bytes), including the issued frame intent; no matching owned process remained.
++The later audit found its G0 model directory missing, so this count does not
++establish complete original retention.
++The cheap diagnostic stack timer is disclosed; no per-call profiler was used
